==Etymology==
"Blitzwolfer" is a rearrangement of the CNN newscaster [[Wolf Blitzer]]'s name. [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] renamed the transformation after briefly seeing Wolf Blitzer on television.<ref name="AABiL" />

Mostly from the word "Blitz" a sudden, fast attack, like how wolves attack. Wolf, and "Woofer" a type of loudspeaker designed to reproduce low frequencies, referencing how wolves use sounds like when their growling.

==Trivia==
*[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] originally called his [[Loboan (Classic)|Loboan]] form "Benwolf" because he thought the transformation was permanent.<ref name="Benwolf" /> 
**Consequently, this makes Blitzwolfer one of the four aliens whose working name had Ben's name in it; the other three being [[Snare-Oh]], [[Frankenstrike]], and [[Nanomech]].
**Benwolf was eventually renamed "Blitzwolfer" to avoid embarrassment after [[Kai Green|Kai]] asked him if the alien was still called "Benwolf".<ref name="AABiL" />
**[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] came up with the working name Blitzwolfer, and it ended up being used as no one else came up with a better name.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Came Up With Blitzwolfer.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Nyancy Chan]] and her cats are afraid of Blitzwolfer.<ref name="Catfight" />
*Kai is fond of Blitzwolfer and thinks he is cute in a pet-like way.<ref name="AABiL" /><ref name="SoDS" />
*Kai has a photo of Blitzwolfer for [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben's]] number on her cell phone.<ref name="SoDS" />
*Blitzwolfer's voice in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' is simply [[Tara Strong]]'s normal performance as Ben but pitch-shifted down.
**This is confirmed due to one of her lines as Blitzwolfer reappearing in the recap of ''[[Be Afraid of the Dark]]'' with no added effects.
*[[Duncan Rouleau]] once stated that Blitzwolfer's sonic howls are more powerful than [[Echo Echo]]'s sonic screams.{{Refn|[[:File:Blitzwolfer's Powerful Howl.png]]|group = DR}} He later did not recall making the original statement, elaborating that the answer to the question depends on what the story needs.{{Refn|[[:File:Blitzwolfer's Howls vs Echo Echo Sonic Screams New Response.png]]|group = DR}}
*In the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''', Blitzwolfer's tongue retracted and stowed itself away when his muzzle split.{{Refn|[[:File:Blitzwolfer's Tongue.PNG]]|group = TNP}} This is changed in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', as his tongue stays in place and splits in half.<ref name="SoDS" />
*Blitzwolfer's '''Original Series''' design was made by [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]],{{Refn|[[:File:Tom Designed S3 & S4 Characters.png]]|group = TNP}} while his '''Omniverse''' appearance was designed by [[Steven Choi]].{{Refn|[[:File:OV Blitzwolfer and Snare-Oh Designers.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*Despite appearing in the [[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)/Theme Song|theme song]], 11-year-old Blitzwolfer was not necessarily planned to appear in '''Omniverse''' flashbacks.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Young Ben Aliens From Intro.png]]|group = DJW}}
*In a former ''[[FusionFall]]'' Halloween event, Dracula sold the outfits of Blitzwolfer along with Snare-oh and Frankenstrike.

